---
source: system/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"pipesz\")"
---
Set or examine pipe and FIFO buffer sizes.

Uses fcntl(2) with F_GETPIPE_SZ and F_SETPIPE_SZ to get or set the buffer sizes of pipes and FIFOs.

Usage: pipesz [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]...

Arguments:
  [COMMAND]...
          Command to execute after setting pipe sizes

Options:
  -g, --get
          Report pipe buffer sizes

  -s, --set <SET>
          Set pipe buffer size in bytes

  -f, --file <FILE>
          Operate on a FIFO/pipe at this path (repeatable)

  -n, --fd <FD>
          Operate on this file descriptor number (repeatable)

  -i, --stdin
          Shorthand for --fd 0

  -o, --stdout
          Shorthand for --fd 1

  -e, --stderr
          Shorthand for --fd 2

  -c, --check
          Exit immediately on any error

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-fatal warnings

  -v, --verbose
          Emit headers (get) or print actual sizes (set)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
